.nh
.TH "FGT" "1" "Sep 2026" "fgt" "fgt Manual"

.SH NAME
fgt-api - Make a raw authenticated API call (escape hatch)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfgt api   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Issue an arbitrary call against the FortiOS REST API, handling auth, base
URL, TLS and VDOM for you. The path is relative to /api/v2/, so use
cmdb/... for configuration and monitor/... for status. Use this for
endpoints the curated commands don't cover yet — every endpoint is reachable.

.PP
For a mutating method (POST/PUT/DELETE) you are prompted to confirm first
(pass --yes to skip). Write bodies are JSON: pass --body '\&' / --body
@file.json, or build a flat object with repeated --data key=value.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	raw JSON request body, or @file.json

.PP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--data\fP=[]
	request parameter key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for api


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--column\fP=[]
	select/order output columns (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--context\fP=""
	config context to use

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log request/response metadata to stderr

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--format\fP=""
	output format: table|json|yaml|csv|value

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	skip TLS verification (footgun)

.PP
\fB--no-headers\fP[=false]
	omit table/csv headers

.PP
\fB--password\fP=""
	admin password for session auth (prefer a secret_ref or FGT_CLI_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	config profile to use

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	FortiGate API base URL (e.g. https://fw.example.com)

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	sort by column (NAME[:asc|desc])

.PP
\fB--tls-fingerprint\fP=""
	pin the server cert SHA-256 fingerprint

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	REST API token (prefer a config secret_ref or FGT_CLI_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--user\fP=""
	admin username for session auth (or FGT_CLI_USER)

.PP
\fB--vdom\fP=""
	target VDOM (default: device global/root)

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	do not truncate wide table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	assume yes for destructive confirmations


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  fgt api GET cmdb/firewall/address
  fgt api GET monitor/system/interface
  fgt api POST cmdb/firewall/address --data name=web --data subnet="10.0.0.0 255.255.255.0"
  fgt api PUT cmdb/firewall/address/web --body '{"comment":"updated"}'
  fgt api DELETE cmdb/firewall/address/web
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfgt(1)\fP
